From: Patronus <patronus@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] backport-include/net/sock.h: stable 6.12.119 already has sk_requests_wifi_status()

linux-6.12.119 (stable) carries the 6.16 helper sk_requests_wifi_status() in include/net/sock.h;
the backports header defined it again for every kernel < 6.16 ("redefinition" error building
cfg80211). Skip our copy on the stable 6.12 series from .119 on.

---
--- a/backport-include/net/sock.h
+++ b/backport-include/net/sock.h
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #define sk_error_report(sk) LINUX_BACKPORT(sk_error_report(sk))
 #endif /* <= 5.14 */
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,16,0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,16,0) && !(LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(6,12,119) && LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,13,0))
 static inline bool
 sk_requests_wifi_status(struct sock *sk)
 {
